notes.content:
- A major upgrade in the sensor system: it is now possible to track materials you had in the past, even though you spent it all;
- A fix in the autosave system;

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/38329202/4cf0b75a166e9d156d07367e27aef91590c7d11c.gif[/img]

We are very happy to announce a new update. It fix bugs and fulfill some players requests.

Dear Home version 1.0.2 includes the following changes:

- Initial inventory capacity increased from 10 to 20;
- More effects on woodcutting;
- Clay slopes building is easier;
- Changed iron graphics to make it look more different from stone;
- Fixed map pieces quest;
- Fixed some physics trouble to climb up slopes;
- Fixed black hole making world disappear;

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/38329202/71b86ffebc29d7c8cdde49942e4c174737f0ee79.gif[/img]

Dear Home version 1.0.1 includes the following changes:

- Graphics improvements to better understand puzzles;
- Fixed game menu bug showing ghost inventory;
- Fixed bug allowing players to leave stone circle before drill update.


